## What I did

Gave apply_patch the same dir-taking seam Day 174 gave suggest_related_files:

• **`apply_patch_in(root, path, check_only)** carries the body. The existence probe is root.join(path).exists(), and every git invocation routes through a new local git_output_in(root, args)`.
• `apply_patch(path, check_only)` is now a one-line Path::new(".") wrapper — every production call site (handle_apply, `apply_patch_from_string`) is untouched.
• The `-C` trap: git_output_in prepends -C <root> as a git global, before the subcommand. The strategy ladder's own `-C1 relaxation still sits *after* apply, so both -C` forms coexist in one argv and neither is the other. I checked the no-op claim empirically rather than asserting it — git -C . apply --stat produced byte-identical output to git apply --stat, including for a relative patch path.
• 5 tests converted (7 `set_current_dir lines): the four setup_git_repo users — the helper now returns (TempDir, file_path) and never moves the process — plus test_apply_patch_from_string_valid_in_git_repo`.
• All 5 `#[serial]` attributes deleted with the chdirs, per the Day-174 precedent that leaving them keeps a false record of which tests are dangerous. That left the file with zero, so the now-dead use serial_test::serial; went too.

## Verification

cargo fmt --check, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, build, test — all green, 5047 passed. grep -n "env::set_current_dir(" src/commands_file.rs → nothing.

## The new count

CLAUDE.md's out-of-scope sentence now reads 5 of the original 22, down from 12 — 2 in `dispatch_sub.rs, 2 in commands_git.rs`, and the production `/cd` site in `dispatch.rs`. A fix that falsifies a cardinality owes the new count, so I ran the grep rather than doing the arithmetic in my head.

I did not touch the other three sites — different seams, separate task — and I'm not claiming this fixes the `setup::tests` flake in the trajectory. Both of those tests already use an absolute tempdir, the obvious CWD explanation doesn't obviously fit, and the originating log has expired. This removes a real race; whether it removes that one is unproven.
